Chapter: InductionParse

 Stage 4b/5 of the proof system: the `for all (x : T), P` claim form and
 the `induction on x` proof body are parsed, and the obligation is
 CHECKED by structural subgoal generation (delta/iota over each
 constructor, with an inductive hypothesis at every recursive field) and
 erased at emit (CDX4020). For `add n Zero === n`: the Zero case reduces
 to `Zero === Zero` (Refl); the Succ case reduces to
 `Succ (add k Zero) === Succ k`, discharged by `cong ih` where the
 inductive hypothesis ih is `add k Zero === k`. This is a real proof,
 not an unproven axiom.

Section: Nat

  Nat =
   | Zero
   | Succ (Nat)

  add : Nat, Nat -> Nat
  add (a) (b) = when a
   is Zero -> b
   is Succ (n) -> Succ (add n b)

Section: Proof

  claim add-zero : for all (n : Nat), add n Zero === n
  proof add-zero =
   induction on n
    is Zero -> Refl
    is Succ (k) (ih) -> cong ih
   qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "induction-parse ok"
  end
